  "worked_solution": "The function $M(t)$ models the decay rate for the particles $t$ microseconds since observations started.\n\nThus, the decay rate of the muons after $0.5$ microseconds is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(0.5) & =2\\cdot {e}^{-2(0.5)} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {e}^{-1} \\\\  & \u22480.736.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the decay rate of the particles is $0.736$ muons per microsecond.",
